  "body": "Otis Bardwell drives a reconstructed occupied wagon circuit in 1835, and Hans Johnson drives a Brougham circuit in 1904, in Full or Balanced detail. Walk up and use Interact to Stop or Continue; Step back checks visitor clearance. Driver picks and Find use the named person and the vehicle\u2019s current position. Light retires the occupied assembly and restores standing-person ownership.\n\nThe latest pushed increment is `7d75789f9c2d5dc91aab4227d20e20f0677c6cf9`, TREE `9c4550f9f49dd33a9b4d5262b92cf25a234f5ed2`. It integrates current DEV and prepares the Navigator\u2019s registered Inspector module alongside driver-card metadata. The later selection reuses that module, preserving loading deduplication, competing-selection ownership and failed-load retry. Preparation creates no panel or seen marker and does not open the device.\n\nEarlier startup changes prioritize cooperative route continuations and overlap eligible code imports with the complete static route proof; models still wait for validation. The People pane preserves its household, reader, pictures, citations and review flags while avoiding an unrelated global building-liberties wait. Other tabs retain their original dependency barriers. CI checkout changes retain complete native inputs, commands, decisions, quality settings and original limits.\n\nValidation and remaining delivery work:\n\n- The exact current TREE passed all nine targeted/report checks in the app checkout, including the Navigator\u2019s existing Hans/census cases and new preload, import-deduplication, selection-race and retry cases. Native publication/validation passed before committing this identical tree. All five actual-commit QA checks, whitespace and normal push passed; independent Git and PR readback verify the exact new commit.\n- Independent merge review preserved all 338 one-sided paths and both sides of the shared authored files. The subsequent ledger update changes only the gzip platform byte; its entire compressed payload and decoded JSON are exact. The native affected-tail rebuild timed out at 600 seconds during its second pass; that remains a retained negative, not a fixed-point PASS.\n- On previous public HEAD `d0671d8`, the complete nine-job frame workflow passed both still-frame jobs, all six ordinary memory jobs and its separate intentional-failure self-test. Those are historical results for that HEAD, not measurements of `7d75789`.\n- The previous 1904 phone interaction run mounted its actual driver, then timed out at the original card wait. Per-poll traces show the Navigator still at Home/closed during that window; the correct hydrated card appears later. The failure is preserved. The new preload fix still needs its own published phone result, Find/Light checks, Stop/Continue scopes and desktop verification.\n- Conflicts are now resolved on GitHub. Current-HEAD CI and all four native local preflight parts remain pending. Current-source checks and actual interaction verification remain required before DEV merge.\n\n[Earlier immutable checkpoint and retained failures](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/0c0db297bc925a10b3fdb1ffe16e55bde3163079/evidence/transport-pr1649-incremental-d067-2026-11-03-2320Z/MANIFEST.json).\n\nThis is incremental driving and interaction work. Broader photographic appearance, anatomy, gait, boarding, riding and natural seated animation remain open. The separate driver look-motion preparation is not included. No broader ticket completion or production deployment is claimed.\n",
